AB  - Contemporary design challenges require innovative approaches to generate sustainable and structurally robust furniture, urging the integration of biomimetic principles through Large Language Models and multi-agent simulations. This study introduces a multi-agent framework utilizing an fine-tuned model explicitly with biomimetic datasets, aiming to enhance design fidelity across morphological, functional, and ecological dimensions. Through rigorous evaluation employing novel biomimetic metrics, we observed commendable accuracy in entity recognition with high performance, yet notable deficits emerged in functional fidelity and lifecycle completeness. These findings underscore critical strengths and explicit limitations in current multi-agentic-driven biomimetic generation, directing attention toward necessary refinements to realize well formulated sustainable, biologically inspired design methodologies.
